From 7d7278d7fc54fe43bd458cbc00bd617adacd73f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 17:35:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add parent onboarding (multi-child) and derive curriculum
 week from enrolment
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Parents can now add/manage multiple children via /parent/children instead of
every page hard-coding the single demo child (GET/POST /api/children). The
child and parent-dashboard pages accept ?childId= to switch between them.

Also replaces the hard-coded term=1/week=1 in the session API with
computeCurrentTermWeek(), derived from a new User.enrolledAt column. Clamped
to term 1 / week 1 for now since that's the only week with real curriculum
sequence + item content — verified a long-enrolled child still gets a
non-empty session instead of landing on an empty future week.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0165eXNKUVcmbijWeTYPurQ8
